88: \subsection{Proposed System Overview}
89: The system is a staged pipeline with two phases. The \emph{ingestion phase} (Fig.~\ref{fig:ingestion}) turns raw ARXML into a \emph{reduced graph} --- the typed model, the influence graph, the role assignment, and per-hop authentication. The \emph{analysis phase} (Fig.~\ref{fig:analysis}) runs on \emph{two} reduced graphs (before and updated): structural diff, reachability comparison, finding classification into nine categories, ISO/SAE~21434-style severity scoring, the release gate, and the report. All stage wiring lives in a single auditable \texttt{pipeline.run} function so the CLI, tests, and CI wrapper cannot reassemble stages differently.
