246: \subsection{Algorithm Explanation}
247: Steps 1--8 build the reduced graph for one snapshot; running them twice keeps before and updated strictly symmetric. The index (step~2) is built by generic recursion over any element with a \textsc{short-name}, which is exactly how AUTOSAR forms the absolute paths used in references, so index keys match reference bodies verbatim; unresolved references are recorded as limitations rather than aborting the analysis. Step~6 is where the three-valued result is decided (Algorithm~\ref{alg:secoc}). Step~8 computes, per snapshot, the set of entry-to-critical paths; comparing the two sets yields \emph{newly reachable} pairs and \emph{changed routes}, which are strictly stronger evidence than ``a connector was added.'' Steps~11--14 form the judgement layer, kept in single modules so the finding rule set and the gate policy are reviewable independently of the analysis code.
