228: \section{Implementation}
229: \label{sec:impl}
230: 
231: \subsection{System Architecture and Interfaces}
232: \label{subsec:impl-overview}
233: 
234: The system is implemented in Python~$\geq 3.10$ as a modular package comprising 21 core modules (approx.~6,100 lines of analysis logic) supported by a 401-test verification suite (approx.~2,300 lines).
235: The system requires four external libraries: \texttt{lxml} for parsing, \texttt{networkx} for graph representation and path algorithms, \texttt{PyYAML} for configuration files, and \texttt{matplotlib} for optional graph rendering.
236: Three operational interfaces are provided:
237: (i) a command-line interface (\texttt{arxml-secdiff}) returning process exit codes $0$--$3$ for CI integration;
238: (ii) a programmatic Python API for automated workflows; and
239: (iii) an interactive desktop GUI (developed via Tkinter) for visual inspection of differential attack paths.
240: 
241: \subsection{Schema-Agnostic XML Parsing}
242: \label{subsec:impl-parse}
243: 
244: AUTOSAR R3.x and R4.x revisions alter XML namespace URIs.
245: To maintain version independence, the parser strips all namespace qualifiers immediately after tree ingestion, matching downstream elements solely on local tag names.
246: A recursive indexing pass constructs a unified path index mapping absolute slash-delimited AUTOSAR paths to elements.
247: Cross-package references resolve via dictionary lookups; unresolved external references (such as unbundled vendor platform types) are cataloged as analysis limitations rather than aborting the pipeline.
